1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:05,620
Magnification in mirrors. Image size, orientation, and the formula

2
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:08,171
m equals minus v over u.

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:10,656
One candle, and many possible images. The image can

4
00:00:10,656 --> 00:00:14,000
be enlarged. It can be the same size. Or

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,142
it can be diminished. And sometimes the image is

6
00:00:18,142 --> 00:00:21,907
turned upside down: inverted. Can one number describe both

7
00:00:21,907 --> 00:00:25,340
the size and the orientation? Yes. It is called

8
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:27,751
the magnification, m.

9
00:00:28,327 --> 00:00:31,820
Heights have signs too. Measured upward from the principal

10
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:35,340
axis, the object height, h o, is positive. An

11
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:39,527
upright image also has a positive height, h i.

12
00:00:39,527 --> 00:00:43,690
If the image is inverted, its height is measured

13
00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:48,627
downward, so h i is negative. Upward height: plus.

14
00:00:48,627 --> 00:00:50,518
Downward height: minus.

15
00:00:51,113 --> 00:00:54,943
Now let us build the idea of magnification. Magnification

16
00:00:54,943 --> 00:00:57,031
is the height of the image divided by the

17
00:00:57,031 --> 00:01:00,725
height of the object. In symbols, m equals h

18
00:01:00,725 --> 00:01:03,853
i over h o. If the object is four

19
00:01:03,853 --> 00:01:07,151
centimetres tall and the image is eight, then eight

20
00:01:07,151 --> 00:01:09,961
over four is two. The image is two times

21
00:01:09,961 --> 00:01:11,444
as tall as the object.

22
00:01:12,147 --> 00:01:14,991
The magnitude of m tells us the size. If

23
00:01:14,991 --> 00:01:16,722
the absolute value of m is greater than one,

24
00:01:16,722 --> 00:01:20,457
the image is enlarged. If it equals one, the

25
00:01:20,457 --> 00:01:22,887
image is the same size. If it is less

26
00:01:22,887 --> 00:01:25,512
than one, the image is diminished. So ignore the

27
00:01:25,512 --> 00:01:28,002
sign for a moment: the absolute value of m

28
00:01:28,002 --> 00:01:28,938
tells the size.

29
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:31,577
The sign of m tells us the orientation. Take

30
00:01:31,577 --> 00:01:36,279
an upright object. If the image is upright, h

31
00:01:36,279 --> 00:01:39,197
i is positive, so m is positive. The image

32
00:01:39,197 --> 00:01:42,704
is erect. Now flip the image. Its size does

33
00:01:42,704 --> 00:01:45,547
not change, but h i becomes negative, so m

34
00:01:45,547 --> 00:01:49,975
becomes negative. The image is inverted. The absolute value

35
00:01:49,975 --> 00:01:52,017
of m gives the size, and the sign of

36
00:01:52,017 --> 00:01:53,758
m gives the orientation.

37
00:01:54,207 --> 00:01:56,355
Why can we also write m equals minus v

38
00:01:56,355 --> 00:02:00,895
over u? The textbook compares the two similar triangles

39
00:02:00,895 --> 00:02:04,040
formed by the object and the image at the

40
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:06,907
pole of the mirror. The height ratio turns into

41
00:02:06,907 --> 00:02:09,737
minus v over u. So m equals h i

42
00:02:09,737 --> 00:02:13,067
over h o, which equals minus v over u.

43
00:02:13,067 --> 00:02:17,398
Size information can come from heights, or from distances.

44
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,100
Let us continue the textbook example from the last

45
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:24,207
video. The object height is plus four centimetres, u

46
00:02:24,207 --> 00:02:27,560
is minus twenty five, and v is minus thirty

47
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:30,360
seven point five. Start with h i over h

48
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:35,640
o equals minus v over u. Substitute: h i

49
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:39,540
over four equals minus, minus thirty seven point five

50
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:42,654
over minus twenty five. The two minus signs inside

51
00:02:42,654 --> 00:02:47,220
cancel, leaving only the leading minus: minus thirty seven

52
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:50,431
point five over twenty five. That is minus one

53
00:02:50,431 --> 00:02:53,340
point five. So m equals minus one point five.

54
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:56,456
Then h i equals m times h o, minus

55
00:02:56,456 --> 00:02:58,969
one point five times four. So h i equals

56
00:02:58,969 --> 00:03:00,471
minus six centimetres.

57
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:03,700
Now read the answer physically. The size first: six

58
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:06,772
is greater than four, so the image is enlarged.

59
00:03:06,772 --> 00:03:09,120
Now the sign: the minus tells us the image

60
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:13,898
is below the principal axis. It is inverted. In

61
00:03:13,898 --> 00:03:17,664
terms of magnification: the absolute value of m is

62
00:03:17,664 --> 00:03:21,060
one point five, greater than one, so enlarged. And

63
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:23,991
m is negative, so inverted. Minus one point five

64
00:03:23,991 --> 00:03:26,295
does not mean smaller. The size comes from the

65
00:03:26,295 --> 00:03:28,131
absolute value, one point five.

66
00:03:28,773 --> 00:03:33,293
Your turn. Decode the magnification. A: m equals plus

67
00:03:33,293 --> 00:03:37,453
two. What are the size and the orientation? B:

68
00:03:37,453 --> 00:03:41,783
m equals minus zero point five. C: m equals

69
00:03:41,783 --> 00:03:45,902
minus one. D: u is minus twenty centimetres and

70
00:03:45,902 --> 00:03:49,933
v is minus forty centimetres. Find m. Take your

71
00:03:49,933 --> 00:03:52,044
time, and pause the video if you need to.

72
00:04:03,447 --> 00:04:05,761
Let us check. A: the absolute value of m

73
00:04:05,761 --> 00:04:09,147
is two, so enlarged. And m is positive, so

74
00:04:09,147 --> 00:04:12,404
erect. B: the absolute value is zero point five,

75
00:04:12,404 --> 00:04:17,827
so diminished. And m is negative, so inverted. C:

76
00:04:17,827 --> 00:04:20,151
the absolute value is one, so the same size.

77
00:04:20,151 --> 00:04:24,607
And m is negative, so inverted. D: m equals

78
00:04:24,607 --> 00:04:26,903
minus v over u, which is minus two. The

79
00:04:26,903 --> 00:04:30,618
image is two times enlarged, and inverted.

80
00:04:31,273 --> 00:04:33,863
Here is how to decode m. Question one: how

81
00:04:33,863 --> 00:04:37,861
big is the image? Look only at the absolute

82
00:04:37,861 --> 00:04:42,080
value of m. Greater than one: enlarged. Equal to

83
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:46,553
one: same size. Less than one: diminished. Question two:

84
00:04:46,553 --> 00:04:49,653
which way does the image point? Positive m: erect.

85
00:04:49,653 --> 00:04:54,620
Negative m: inverted. In our example, m is minus

86
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:58,313
one point five: enlarged, and inverted. The magnitude of

87
00:04:58,313 --> 00:05:02,013
m gives the size. The sign of m gives

88
00:05:02,013 --> 00:05:05,553
the orientation. So do not just calculate m. Read

89
00:05:05,553 --> 00:05:08,473
what m is telling you. Thank you for watching,

90
00:05:08,473 --> 00:05:11,144
and see you in the next lesson.
